### Test Health Endpoint
GET http://localhost:8000/health

###

### 1. Create a Payment
POST http://localhost:8000/payments/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subscription_id": 1,
  "amount": 100,
  "gateway_id": "test_gateway"
}

###

### 2. Approve the Payment (Replace {payment_id} with actual ID from step 1)
POST http://localhost:8000/payments/1/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotency_key": "unique-key-123"
}

###

### 3. Refund the Payment (Replace {payment_id} with actual ID from step 1)
POST http://localhost:8000/payments/1/refund
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotency_key": "refund-key-456"
}

###

### 4. Test Idempotency - Try approving same payment again
POST http://localhost:8000/payments/1/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotency_key": "unique-key-123"
}

###

### 5. Create another payment for race condition testing
POST http://localhost:8000/payments/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subscription_id": 1,
  "amount": 50.0,
  "gateway_id": "race_test_gw"
}

###

### 6. Test Notifications - Create a notification
POST http://localhost:8000/notifications/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "family_id": 1,
  "type": "payment_approved",
  "message": "Payment has been approved",
  "data": {"payment_id": 1, "amount": 100}
}

###

### 7. Get all notifications for a family
GET http://localhost:8000/notifications/family/1

###

### 8. Create Payment with Different Gateway
POST http://localhost:8000/payments/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subscription_id": 1,
  "amount": 75.5,
  "gateway_id": "stripe_test"
}

###

### 9. Test Invalid Payment Approval (non-existent payment)
POST http://localhost:8000/payments/99999/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotency_key": "test-invalid-payment"
}

###

### 10. Test Empty/Invalid Data
POST http://localhost:8000/payments/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subscription_id": 999,
  "amount": -10,
  "gateway_id": ""
}
